# UX-SPEC.md § Card detail · ADR 0023 · TESTING-HARNESS.md §3 (`card_detail.*`, `card.properties`)
# — the card detail is a sheet docked to the right of the board, and it is worked by pointer end
# to end: a double-click on a tile opens it, a click on a property row opens the picker `⏎` opens
# there, the board's field keys answer on the card on show, `⌃⏎` posts a comment, and both the
# sheet's ✕ and a click on the dimmed board beside it close it, as `esc` does.
#
# The oracle for the edit is `card.properties`, the property column as the sheet draws it: row 1
# is Priority on a board nobody automated (Status, Priority, Assignee, …), and its one badge is
# the value the daemon wrote back.
#
# Virtual-lane only: it clicks and takes shots.
fixture: board
await idle 20000
key g b
await hub_tab == Board 10000
assert lists.board.rows[2].badges[0] == "1"

# A double-click on a tile opens that card — the pointer twin of `⏎`.
click left 2 board.column[2].card[0]
await overlay == Dialog 10000
await idle 10000
assert dialog.name == CardDetail
assert targets["card_detail.close"] exists && targets["sheet.close"] exists
assert targets["card_detail.property[1]"] exists && targets["card_detail.menu"] exists
assert lists["card.properties"].rows[0].label == "Status"
assert lists["card.properties"].rows[1].label == "Priority"
assert lists["card.properties"].rows[1].badges[0] == "–"

# `c` focuses the composer, `⌃⏎` posts, and the comment lands under the card's prose.
key c
type Keep the fake for the headless lane.
key ctrl-enter
await idle 20000
await targets["card_detail.comment"] exists 15000
shot card-detail

# A click on the Priority row opens the Card property picker `⏎` opens there; a click on a value
# applies it and hands the keyboard back to the sheet.
click card_detail.property[1]
await dialog.name == CardPicker 10000
assert targets["dialog.row[1]"] exists
click dialog.row[1]
await dialog.name == CardDetail 15000
await idle 20000
await lists["card.properties"].rows[1].badges[0] == "High" 15000
shot card-detail-priority

# The board's own field key answers on the card on show: `a` opens the Assignee picker.
key a
await dialog.name == CardPicker 10000
key escape
await dialog.name == CardDetail 10000

# A click on the dimmed board beside the sheet closes it, as `esc` does.
click 120 400
await overlay absent 10000
assert hub_tab == Board

# `⏎` opens the same card again; the sheet's ✕ closes it.
key enter
await dialog.name == CardDetail 10000
click card_detail.close
await overlay absent 10000
dump closed
quit
